commit 27ee4b3 (fix applied; same caveat as g2-before.out)
command node tools/repro/g2-envelope-crash-not-exception.mjs
a1) intake-shape check (admit)      : returned true
a2) validEnvelope (plan exception?): THROWS "refused: key/signature hex"
a3) envelopeRecipient (signer/dest): THROWS "refused: key/signature hex"
b1) validEnvelope (plan exception?): returned {"ciphertext_hash":"ebb5ff8e0a05c0e9837057d3384e305a362f2f19
b2) envelopeRecipient (signer/dest): returned null
c1) validEnvelope (plan exception?): returned {"ciphertext_hash":"ebb5ff8e0a05c0e9837057d3384e305a362f2f19
c2) envelopeRecipient (signer/dest): returned null

In all three cases the row is NOT exception-queued by settle/plan.ts (validEnvelope neither returns false
nor is the decryptability ever probed there); the throw escapes to the process boundary, so ONE such bid
halts the entire settlement (all refunds, the seller payout, stranded in the FROST vault) until someone
edits state by hand.
